Operator: 'crack tn36's tool palette and solve it.' DONE.

THE MECHANIC (fully RE'd): tn36 is a 5-slot MOVE-PROGRAM editor. The object runs a
program vkuvtkaerv where each slot is a command code (tn36.py:2171 okllwtboml:
0=settle,1=left,2=right,3=down,5/6/7/16=rotate,8/9=scale,14/15/63=property,33=up;
step size CSPOIQWER=4). Win = object matches target on 5 attributes (x,y,scale,
rotation,sjmtdfxdrc).

THE TOOL PALETTE (cracked): each slot has TWO bit-buttons at (slotX,y=41)+(slotX,y=44):
button1=+1, button2=+2, clicking BOTH sets the slot to code 3 (down). Slot centers
x~{19,24,31,34,39}. RUN by clicking the object sub-button sxhtkytekm (~36,55).

L1 SOLVE (7 clicks, reproduction-gated reproduced=True L1): the given program
[3,0,3,0,0] only reaches y=21 (2 downs x4); edit slots 1,3,4 to code 3 ->
[3,3,3,3,3] = 5 downs x4 = +20 -> y:13->33 = WIN. Trajectory:
results/arc_explore_trajectory_tn36.json. Registry: tn36 reproduced L1;
reproducible_total 15->16 levels, 12->13 games.

This is the deep-tail per-game RE that the engine-A/B predicted is the real lever
(not a search-engine swap) -- a genuinely new game solved by understanding its
mechanic.
